flowchart TB
    accTitle: Product X grounding interactions
    accDescr: A book-created incident example showing two separate external interactions: a digital service query and a question to an on-call engineer. Each may provide an observation for working memory.

    WM[Current incident information]
    WM --> QUERY[Digital grounding: query health or deployment status]
    QUERY --> SERVICE[Payment service or dashboard]
    SERVICE -->|result, if returned| OBS1[Digital observation]
    WM --> ASK[Dialogue grounding: ask about a recent change]
    ASK --> ENGINEER[On-call engineer]
    ENGINEER -->|reply, if received| OBS2[Dialogue observation]
    OBS1 --> ACTIVE[Working memory updated with available observations]
    OBS2 --> ACTIVE

    classDef store fill:#EEF7EE,stroke:#27AE60,color:#1C1C1E,stroke-width:1.5px;
    classDef action fill:#EAF4FB,stroke:#1A4A8A,color:#1C1C1E,stroke-width:1.3px;
    classDef environment fill:#F4F4F4,stroke:#888888,color:#1C1C1E,stroke-width:1.2px;
    class WM,ACTIVE,OBS1,OBS2 store;
    class QUERY,ASK action;
    class SERVICE,ENGINEER environment;
